`rich/repr.py` seems to be the core logic for generating rich representations (`__repr__`) based on a custom `__rich_repr__` method or by inspecting `__init__`.

The issue description mentions "Fix record and capture". This sounds like a problem where the state of an object, especially when it contains complex types or is being captured for logging/display, might be lost or incorrectly represented.

If I look at the structure of `auto_repr` in `rich/repr.py`:
```python
